<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Watches the proposer's *progress*, not its liveness.

  KeepAlive restarts a process that exits. It cannot see a process that is
  still running but has stopped producing thoughts - a wedged socket, a model
  server that accepts and never answers. That silence is the same failure mode
  that has already bitten this colony twice, so the signal here is the mtime of
  think-ledger.jsonl. No growth for 600s (4x the 150s round interval, ~120x a
  normal round's cost) => kick the supervisor. The kick is logged, and a
  cooldown stops an unfixed stall from turning into restart noise.

  The same timer also carries the *voter* check. tools/vote_watchdog.py can
  see a reactor answering a frozen point in the past - process up, stances
  varying, panel green, every target stamped hours ago - because it fits the
  answer-lag slope instead of an age threshold. It shipped and then sat unused
  for a day: a signal with no caller is a docstring. So the caller lives here,
  on a timer that already exists, and exit 2 becomes a claimable [alarm] task
  in the mailbox rather than one more unread log line. A wedge only pages once;
  the state file remembers first-seen and forgets a member that recovers.

  The third leg asks whether the code that produced the thought is the code the
  fleet is on. capability.code_head is stamped at boot, so it reads the *running*
  process, not the checkout: on 2026-10-19 win was frozen ~51 commits back and
  its decision member answered ~39-hour-old proposals while every panel stayed
  green. code_drift_check.py measures that drift behind a grace window (a push
  makes the whole fleet briefly behind, which is not a fault), and this timer
  turns a drift that persists into a claimable [alarm] code-drift task. It
  shares the state file with the vote leg, scoped by alarm family.

  The win root is read over the tailnet (100.93.216.90), not over the LAN.
  macOS 27 grants local-network reachability per *responsible process*, and for
  a launchd job that runs the Homebrew interpreter, that process is the
  interpreter: the job gets Errno 65 on its own socket for 192.168.31.x, and
  curl rc=7 for a curl *spawned by* it, because a child inherits the refusal
  from its parent. Measured from launchd jobs on 2026-10-19: a job led by
  /bin/sh reaches the LAN fine, and so does a /usr/bin/curl or /usr/bin/ssh it
  spawns directly - but this watchdog's chain starts at the interpreter, so
  swapping the transport inside the tool cannot fix it and re-rooting the job
  would cost it its Python. The tailnet is not "local network" and answers that
  interpreter every time.

  pi5 has no tailnet address, so it is read through a local mirror of its
  /nodes table (the root-json source below), refreshed over ssh every 60s by
  tools/mirror_ledger.py. That copier needs the same /bin/sh root as any other
  LAN reader here, so it is deliberately not a child of this interpreter-led
  job. The mirror is evidence only while it is fresh: past its max-age window
  it is reported unreadable instead, because a dead copier is this Mac's blind
  spot and not a member falling behind. (An XML comment may not contain a
  doubled hyphen, which is why the flags above are named in prose here.)

  Install:
    cp tools/mac-launchd/com.jewelroam.pandosi-think-watchdog.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
    launchctl bootstrap gui/$(id -u) ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.jewelroam.pandosi-think-watchdog.plist
  Inspect:
    tail -f ~/.pandosi/logs/think-watchdog.launchd.out
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>com.jewelroam.pandosi-think-watchdog</string>
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/Users/zhengenrong/Downloads/PandoSI-island/.venv/bin/python</string>
    <string>/Users/zhengenrong/Downloads/PandoSI-island/tools/think_watchdog.py</string>
    <string>--ledger</string>
    <string>/Users/zhengenrong/.pandosi/think-ledger.jsonl</string>
    <string>--stall-seconds</string>
    <string>600</string>
    <string>--cooldown-file</string>
    <string>/Users/zhengenrong/.pandosi/logs/think-watchdog.cooldown</string>
    <string>--restart-cmd</string>
    <string>launchctl kickstart -k gui/501/com.jewelroam.pandosi-think</string>
    <string>--vote-cmd</string>
    <string>/Users/zhengenrong/Downloads/PandoSI-island/.venv/bin/python /Users/zhengenrong/Downloads/PandoSI-island/tools/vote_watchdog.py --url http://127.0.0.1:8776 --token-file /Users/zhengenrong/.pandosi/mailbox.token --decision pandosi-pi5-x --decision pandosi-pi5-laya --decision win-laya-int8 --decision mac-text --decision mac-laya-int8 --sleep-gated-member mac-text --sleep-gated-member mac-laya-int8 --json --state-file /Users/zhengenrong/.pandosi/vote-watchdog-state.json --snapshot-file /Users/zhengenrong/.pandosi/vote-watchdog.json --page-new-only</string>
    <string>--vote-timeout</string>
    <string>120</string>
    <string>--code-cmd</string>
    <string>/Users/zhengenrong/Downloads/PandoSI-island/.venv/bin/python /Users/zhengenrong/Downloads/PandoSI-island/tools/code_drift_check.py --repo /Users/zhengenrong/Downloads/PandoSI-island --root mac http://127.0.0.1:8765 /Users/zhengenrong/.pandosi/pairing.token --root win http://100.93.216.90:8790 /Users/zhengenrong/.pandosi/win-pairing.token --root-json pi5 /Users/zhengenrong/.pandosi/remote/pi5-root.json --state-file /Users/zhengenrong/.pandosi/code-drift-state.json --snapshot-file /Users/zhengenrong/.pandosi/code-drift-check.json --json</string>
    <string>--code-timeout</string>
    <string>120</string>
    <string>--alarm-url</string>
    <string>http://127.0.0.1:8776</string>
    <string>--alarm-token-file</string>
    <string>/Users/zhengenrong/.pandosi/mailbox.token</string>
    <string>--alarm-by</string>
    <string>vote-watchdog</string>
    <string>--alarm-state-file</string>
    <string>/Users/zhengenrong/.pandosi/think-watchdog-alarms.json</string>
    <string>--alarm-refresh-seconds</string>
    <string>21600</string>
    <string>--alarm-overdue-seconds</string>
    <string>43200</string>
    <string>--alarm-note</string>
    <string>members on hosts this Mac cannot reach (win-laya-int8: no shell, no pairing path) cannot be restarted from here; those need a human at that host</string>
  </array>
  <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
  <string>/Users/zhengenrong/Downloads/PandoSI-island</string>
  <key>RunAtLoad</key>
  <false/>
  <key>StartInterval</key>
  <integer>300</integer>
  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>/Users/zhengenrong/.pandosi/logs/think-watchdog.launchd.out</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>/Users/zhengenrong/.pandosi/logs/think-watchdog.launchd.err</string>
</dict>
</plist>
